course: dictionary
lesson: 7717
title: One word, many meanings: public
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word public has more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to find out which one the writer means. Public means for everyone to use or see, not private. «Borrowing books from the public library is free» means anyone can go in and borrow.
explain: The public can also mean ordinary people in general, as in the general public. Public speaking means talking in front of other people. Public transport means buses and trains that are run or paid for by the government.
explain: When you are out in public, in shops, on buses or in parks, stay with your adult. Agree on a meeting point in case you get lost. Never share private information in a public online post.
fact: Public means for everyone to use or see, not private.
fact: The public means ordinary people in general.
fact: «Comfort station» is an official American word for a public toilet, for example in a park.
fact: «Many towns had public bathhouses» in medieval times, so people could go and wash.
fact: Public broadcasters such as the BBC, ABC or CBC are paid for by the public and meant to report freely.
exercise: «Borrowing books from the public library is free.» What does public mean in this sentence? | Very quiet | Paid for by one family only | *Open for everyone to use | Full of people shouting
exercise: Doctors and nurses work in public hospitals, so anyone can get care there. What does public mean here? | *Paid for by the government and open to everyone | Only open at night | Private, only for one family | Used only by doctors
exercise: Which phrase means speaking in front of other people? | *public speaking | quiet reading | secret garden | private letter
test: «Many towns had public bathhouses.» What does public mean here? | Under the sea | Only for the king | *Open for everyone to use | Closed for repairs
test: Which of these is a public service? | *Library | Diary | Bedroom | Secret club
exam: Aiden says public means only for his family. Is he right? | Yes, public means secret | Yes, public always means one family | *No, public means for everyone to use | No, public means dark and empty
